[SIZE="4"][B]About[/B][/SIZE]

This is an unofficial TWRP 3.1.1-1 build for the [B]LG G2 Mini LTE D625[/B] (codename [B]g2mv[/B], NVIDIA Tegra 4i). It uses the unmodified stock LG kernel from firmware D62510c and is built from the Android 4.4 OmniROM/TWRP tree.

[COLOR="Red"][B]Only for the Tegra 4i D625. It will not boot on the Snapdragon G2 Mini models (D620, D618...).[/B][/COLOR]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Requires the patched bootloader.[/B][/COLOR] The stock D625 bootloader refuses unsigned recovery images. Unlock it first:
[URL="PUT_BOOTLOADER_GUIDE_URL_HERE"][GUIDE] How To Unlock the Bootloader LG G2 Mini LTE D625 (Tegra 4i)[/URL]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status[/B][/SIZE]

Tested on real hardware, D625 on firmware D62510c:

[LIST]
[*]Display, touchscreen, brightness and battery level
[*]ADB in recovery
[*]Internal storage and external microSD (vfat)
[*]Backup of System, Data and Boot, including split archives, with MD5 verification
[*]Restore of Boot, System and Data; Android boots afterwards
[*]Backup of the LG/Icera partitions (Modem, Cust, MPT, PST, SNS, RCT, DRM, SEP), byte-identical to raw dumps
[*]Entering recovery with the hardware keys [B]without wiping anything[/B]
[*]Display without USB connected (see the fixes below)
[/LIST]

[B]Not included:[/B] MTP, exFAT and decryption of an encrypted /data. With an encrypted phone, Data cannot be backed up.

[SIZE="4"][B]Device-specific fixes[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Backups no longer hang.[/B] Stock TWRP 3.1.1 froze on every /system backup when the archive was split, because the tar child processes called GUI functions after fork(). A patch removes those calls from all backup and restore children.
[*][B]No white lines without USB.[/B] With the cable unplugged, memory (EMC) dropped to 25.5 MHz and the display controller could not keep up. This build keeps a 102 MHz floor.
[*][B]Safe hardware-key entry.[/B] The only key path goes through LG's "Factory Reset" screen, which tells recovery to wipe /data. This build ignores that request (TW_IGNORE_MISC_WIPE_DATA).
[*][B]Correct partition sizes.[/B] Recovery and boot are 12 MiB (checked against the kernel, the raw GPT and an nvflash readback). The /data crypto footer is taken from MDA, as in the stock fstab.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]

[B]Before starting:[/B] the bootloader must be unlocked, and ADB must be authorized in Android.

[B]1. Test without installing:[/B]
[CODE]adb reboot bootloader
fastboot boot twrp-3.1.1-1-g2mv.img[/CODE]

Check that the display, touch and ADB work.

[B]2. From that temporary TWRP, back up the stock recovery and install TWRP:[/B]
[CODE]adb shell dd if=/dev/block/platform/sdhci-tegra.3/by-name/SOS of=/sdcard/SOS-stock.img
adb pull /sdcard/SOS-stock.img
adb push twrp-3.1.1-1-g2mv.img /tmp/twrp.img
adb shell dd if=/tmp/twrp.img of=/dev/block/platform/sdhci-tegra.3/by-name/SOS bs=4096
adb reboot recovery[/CODE]

The dd method above is the tested one. fastboot flash recovery and TWRP's "Install Image" were not used in testing.

Stock Android does not overwrite TWRP on this firmware: [I]/system/etc/install-recovery.sh[/I] does not exist.

[SIZE="4"][B]Do this first: back up the LG partitions[/B][/SIZE]

Go to [B]Backup[/B], select [B]Modem (MDM), Cust (CST), LG MPT, LG PST, LG SNS, LG RCT, LG DRM and LG SEP[/B], and copy the result to your PC. These hold modem, calibration and carrier data that is unique to your phone and that a ROM flash can destroy.

[COLOR="Red"][B]Never share these backups or the MSC (misc) partition. They contain your IMEI.[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]Entering recovery[/B][/SIZE]

From Android or TWRP:
[CODE]adb reboot recovery[/CODE]

[B]With the keys, phone off.[/B] The usual LG combo does [B]not[/B] work on the D625. This is the sequence the bootloader actually expects:

[LIST=1]
[*][B]Unplug the USB cable.[/B] The combo is ignored while USB is connected.
[*]Hold [B]Volume Down[/B] and keep it held until TWRP appears.
[*]Hold [B]Power[/B] until the LG logo appears, then [B]release Power[/B].
[*]Immediately [B]tap Power 2-3 times[/B]: about 0.3 s pressed and 0.3 s released each time. Quick taps are not counted.
[*]The "Factory Reset" screen is confirmed by the held Volume Down, and TWRP starts.
[/LIST]

[COLOR="Red"][B]The screen says "Factory Reset", but this TWRP does not wipe anything. Do NOT use this key combo with the stock recovery or with another TWRP build: they WILL wipe /data.[/B][/COLOR]

Volume Up with USB connected enters LG download (LAF) mode instead.

[SPOILER="Why this key sequence (technical)"]
Reverse-engineered from the D62510c bootloader (LgeBootMain) and the D625 kernel key table. The power key is the MAX77660 PMIC EN0 input; its GLBINT1 register clears on read: press = EN0_F (0x40), release = EN0_R (0x80), held 1 s = EN0_1SEC (0x20). The bootloader polls it every 150 ms:

[LIST]
[*]Power held for at least 1 s to power on.
[*]Volume Down held and no USB cable at the boot-mode check.
[*]Any new Power event (the release) within 0.75 s.
[*]A clean release within 2.25 s, then another clean release within 2.25 s with Volume Down still held.
[*]The Factory Reset screen: Volume Down confirms, Volume Up cancels.
[/LIST]

A press and release inside the same 150 ms poll read as 0xc0 and are ignored, so the taps must be slow. Full details are in the device tree README.
[/SPOILER]

